Commentary of al-Nasafi (Madarik al-Tanzil) on surah 44, verse 51:

﴿Indeed, the God-fearing will be in a station﴾, with a fatha (on the mim), and it is the place of standing; and what is meant is a place, which is one of the specific terms that has been used in the sense of the general. And with a damma (on the mim), "Madani and Shami" (read it), and it is the place of dwelling;

﴿trustworthy﴾, from "amina al-rajul, amanatan, fa-huwa amin" (the man became secure, in trust, so he is trustworthy), and it is the opposite of the treacherous. So the place is described with it metaphorically, because a frightening place is as though it betrays its companion by what he encounters in it of hardships.
